  "term": "tardive",
  "definition": "Tardive refers to abnormal involuntary movements that develop in connection with the use of certain medications or drugs. These movements can include excessive or reduced movement, tremor, or dystonia, often affecting the face, tongue, neck, trunk, or limbs.",
